.TH DARK-CANARY 1 "2026-09" "dark-canary" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dark-canary \- mirror traffic to a shadow deployment and diff the responses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dark-canary
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dark-canary
sends production traffic to two deployments, compares the responses and reports
whether the shadow behaves identically to the primary. One path returns to the
user; the other is a dead end.
.PP
It runs in either of two shapes. As a
.B proxy
.RB ( \-primary
and
.BR \-shadow )
it fronts both deployments itself. As a
.B capture sink
.RB ( \-listen )
it receives pairs of captures posted by something else \(em an nginx
.B mirror
directive, say \(em and correlates them.
.PP
The diff engine is the product: declarative noise suppression for timestamps,
identifiers, ordering and float precision, so that a report contains real
divergences rather than every field that was never going to match.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Capture and correlation
.TP
.BI \-listen " ADDR"
Address to accept captures on (default 127.0.0.1:8099).
.TP
.BI \-token " TOKEN"
Shared secret required on posted captures.
.TP
.BI \-rules " FILE"
Noise ruleset (YAML), merged on top of the built-in defaults.
.TP
.BI \-correlate\-timeout " DURATION"
How long a lone capture waits for its partner (default 30s).
.TP
.BI \-max\-pending " N"
Bound on unpaired captures held in memory (default 10000).
.TP
.BI \-scrub " FIELDS"
Comma-separated body fields to redact on arrival.
.TP
.BI \-report\-every " DURATION"
Print the report to standard error on this interval (0 = only on request).
.SS Proxying
.TP
.BI \-primary " URL"
Upstream whose response is returned to the caller.
.TP
.BI \-shadow " URL"
Upstream that is mirrored to and discarded, e.g.
.IR http://127.0.0.1:9002 .
.TP
.BI \-proxy\-listen " ADDR"
Address to serve proxied traffic on (default 127.0.0.1:8080).
.TP
.BI \-sample " RATE"
Fraction of traffic mirrored to the shadow.
.TP
.BI \-shadow\-timeout " DURATION"
How long the shadow gets before its response is abandoned (default 10s).
.TP
.BI \-max\-inflight " N"
Bound on concurrent shadow requests (default 64).
.SS Safety
.TP
.BI \-kill\-file " PATH"
Path whose existence stops all processing.
.TP
.BI \-max\-body " BYTES"
Largest capture body accepted.
.TP
.B \-allow\-write\-mirroring
Mirror non-idempotent methods too. Off by default: mirroring a write means the
shadow performs it as well.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 64
A flag, or a combination of flags, the tool refuses.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Front two deployments and mirror a tenth of the traffic:
.PP
.RS
.B dark-canary \-primary http://127.0.0.1:9001 \-shadow http://127.0.0.1:9002 \-sample 0.1
.RE
.PP
Take captures from nginx instead, suppressing known noise:
.PP
.RS
.B dark-canary \-listen 127.0.0.1:8099 \-rules noise.yaml
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/dark-canary
